Viśvāmitra abandons northern quarter and performs thousand-year silent tapas in east --- Viśvāmitra endures wood-like and resists anger despite obstacles --- Gods blinded by his radiance beg Brahmā to avert world destruction --- Brahmā grants Viśvāmitra Brahmanhood and long life with Maruts --- Viśvāmitra asks Ōṃ, Vaṣaṭ and Vēdas to accept him and Vasiṣṭha to befriend him --- Vasiṣṭha befriends Viśvāmitra and confirms his Brahmarṣi status --- Viśvāmitra worships Vasiṣṭha and roams earth with fulfilled desire --- Śatānanda hails Viśvāmitra as embodied tapas before Rāma --- Janaka thanks Viśvāmitra for attending his sacrifice with princes